    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p>The standard medical kit carried by most Jedi, the 8-2A Medical Bundle contains the basic items needed to treat ailments and diseases in a package small enough to fit in a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Utility_Belt\" title=\"Utility Belt\">Utility Belt</a>. Since Jedi can rely on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Force\" title=\"The Force\">The Force</a> to speed up their healing processes, many common items- such as bacta patches and synthetic flesh- are absent from the Medical Bundle. </p><p>A Medical Bundle counts as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medical_Kit\" title=\"Medical Kit\">Medical Kit</a> for the purposes of using the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Treat_Injury\" title=\"Treat Injury\">Treat Injury</a> skill, but only on targets currently in a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Trance\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Trance\">Force Trance</a>. </p>",
